            <ArticleTitle>Postural intermittent headaches as the initial symptom of a cavernoma in the third ventricle.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>105-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cavernous malformations (CM) occur very rarely in the ventricular system. We report a patient with a rare location in the third ventricle who had intermittent headaches as the initial symptom.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
